# What `vercel deploy` uploads from this folder. Vercel hosts only the static
# docs; the app itself runs on a host with a disk (fly.toml, DEPLOY.md
# "Vercel, Fly.io and friends").
#
# vercel.json is plain JSON, which has no comments, so it is explained here:
#   framework: null         no framework ("Other"): Vercel serves files as they are
#   installCommand: ""      skip the install step (there is no package.json)
#   buildCommand: ""        skip the build step: the HTML is committed, built on a
#                           laptop by `python3 scripts/build-tutorial.py`
#   outputDirectory: docs   publish the docs/ folder; docs/index.html (a copy of
#                           docs/tutorial.html) is the page at "/"
#   cleanUrls: true         /tutorial serves tutorial.html; /tutorial.html redirects there
#
# Ignore everything at the top of the repository, then let back in only the
# two things the site needs. This keeps target/ (gigabytes of Rust build output),
# spaces/, src/ and the rest off Vercel.
/*
!docs
!vercel.json
